# High-Fidelity Unified Invoice Printing

## The Issue 📋
Currently, the beautiful UI invoice in `/dashboard/billing/invoice/[id]` changes drastically when `window.print()` is invoked. Tailwind's `print:border-0`, `print:shadow-none`, and aggressively un-styled `@media print` classes completely strip the borders, layout structure, and backgrounds, resulting in a broken paper receipt.

## User Review Required ⚠️
> [!IMPORTANT]  
> Before I proceed, I need to know your target paper size so I can write the exact CSS for it. Do you want the invoice to be designed for standard **A4 paper sheets**, or a small **80mm Thermal Receipt Printer**? I will design the unified template to perfectly fit your choice.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Extract a Unified Template
#### [NEW] [InvoiceTemplate.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/InvoiceTemplate.tsx)
- Extract the complex JSX currently trapped inside the billing page into a reusable Server/Client agnostic component.
- Pass `sale`, `shopSettings`, and `invoiceSettings` as typed React Props.

### 2. Overhaul the Print CSS (`@media print`)
#### [MODIFY] [globals.css](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/globals.css) and component classes
- **Preserve Borders:** Remove all `print:border-0` classes so the crisp "Bill To" cards and tables remain visible on paper.
- **Color Preservation:** Force browsers to print exact colors using `-webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;` and `print-color-adjust: exact;`.
- **Formatting:** Ensure font sizes scale down properly to fit the paper dimensions, and disable printing for the Sidebar/Navbar entirely.
- **Watermark:** Center the watermark cleanly on the page without disrupting text flow.

### 3. Replace the Page Logic
#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/dashboard/billing/invoice/[id]/page.tsx)
- Rip out the enormous 367 lines of raw UI code.
- Import and render `<InvoiceTemplate sale={sale} shopSettings={...} settings={...} />`.
- Retain the clean `window.print()` header buttons (hidden natively during printing).
